# indicator-service-dev-indicator-state-changelog:4 and the heatmap retention override below
# exist because dev's broker runs num.partitions=32 WITH auto-create: on every clean the owning
# service asks for its topic and the broker wins the race, creating it at 32. Kafka Streams then
# refuses to start ("Existing internal topic ... has invalid partitions: expected: 4") and
# StrikeLiquidityStreams refuses on "cannot enforce delete/<=1d retention". Both were repaired by
# hand after three separate dev cleans (2026-08-14/17/18). Declaring them makes the clean create
# them correctly instead. Mirrors the es4 fixes in deploy PR #815 / #846.
OPTIONS_EDGE_TOPICS="indicator-service-dev-indicator-state-changelog:4 options.databento.oi.anchor-manifest:1 options.databento.oi.nowcast.by-strike:4 options.es-strike-intel-spx-aligned:4 rates.sofr.databento-sr3-feed-service.history:1 options.marketdata.selection:1 options.databento.control:1 options.databento.raw:32 options.databento.events.raw:32 options.databento.normalized:32 options.ibkr.raw:32 options.ibkr.display:32 options.ibkr.display.volume.current:32 options.ibkr.display.gamma.history:32 options.ibkr.pace:32 options.ibkr.pace.rank:32 options.ibkr.directional-pressure:32 underlying.vix.price:1 options.ibkr.volume-sandwich.current:32 options.ibkr.volume-sandwich.alerts:32 options.databento.display:32 options.databento.display.volume.current:32 options.databento.display.gamma.history:32 options.databento.pace:32 options.databento.pace.rank:32 options.databento.pace.mission:32 options.databento.directional-pressure:32 options.databento.market-pressure.mission:32 options.databento.sandwich.mission:32 options.databento.volume-sandwich.current:32 options.databento.volume-sandwich.alerts:32 options.databento.volume.state.compacted:32 options.databento.maxpain:4 options.spx.vix-option-inteligence-service.current:32 market.spx.market-carry-service.current:32 options.spx.greek-move-auth.current:4 options.spx.spread-skew.events:4 options.spx.spread-skew.current:4 options.spx.option-truth-engine-service.by-strike:32 options.spx.greek-move-auth.events:4 display.volume.current:32 display.volume.sandwich.current:32 display.volume.sandwich.alerts:32 options.spx.participant-flow:32 options.spx.mission-control.current:32 options.rewind.journal:1 options.rewind.audit:1 strike-liquidity-heatmap-bucket:32 strike-liquidity-heatmap-dashboard:32 underlying.es.trades:32 es.open-direction.forecast:4 es.open-direction.outcome:4 es.open-direction.status:4 options.databento.gex.strike:32 options.databento.gex.strike.history:32 options.databento.gex.strike.preopen:32 options.databento.gex.flow.by-strike:32 options.databento.gex.flow.10s:32 options.databento.gex.flow.1m:32 options.databento.gex.flow.5m:32 options.databento.gex.flow.15m:32 options.databento.gex.flow.session:32 options.databento.gex.flow.dashboard:32 options.databento.gex.magnet:32 options.databento.gex.oi-status:32 spx.basis.state:1 spx.basis.a1.evidence:1 underlying.spx.index.price:1 options.spx.gamma-migration.current:4 options.spx.gamma-migration.scoring:4 options.spx.spot-vol-regime.current:1 options.spx.spot-vol-regime.events:1 options.spx.vol-premium.ivrv:1 options.ibkr.gex.status:1 options.ibkr.gex.strike.shadow:32 options.indicators.snapshot.current:1 options.indicators.bars:8 options.indicators.repartition:4 options.indicators.bootstrap.control:1 options.multileg.observations:4 options.multileg.window.status:4 options.multileg.sr.levels:4"
# options.rewind.journal MUST be single-partition + compacted: the Rewind
# service's hydrate path relies on compaction-keyed-by-run_id and
# single-partition ordering as its consistency model (Journal.hydrate
# refuses to start otherwise).
# options.rewind.audit: append-only audit trail, single partition (key=run_id
# for log-locality). delete cleanup with default retention is acceptable for
# v1; a follow-up PR will set retention.ms=7776000000 (90d) via the
# apply-internal-topic-configs.sh pattern. Audit replay within 24h is also
# served by Loki on the same logs.
# options.databento.gex.strike is compacted (compact,delete): the GEX service creates it via
# ensureCompactedTopic and downstream relies on last-value-per-strike keying. Adding it here so the deploy's
# apply-topics step keeps it compacted (a plain-delete entry would strip compaction). The gex-flow.* and
# gex.magnet topics are plain delete (last-value-wins is served by the consumers), so they are NOT compacted.
# options.databento.gex.strike.preopen is the context tape's pre-open gex source: databento-gex-history
# projects the IBKR pre-open records it keeps OUT of .history (#552) onto this topic. It MUST stay plain
# delete (never compacted): the context tape seeks back and replays it to rebuild pre-open buckets, and
# compaction would drop earlier-bucket values for a strike that updates again pre-open. Retention override
# 259200000 (72h) covers the es4 ~23h GLOBEX pre-open window with margin for a delayed restart.
# (The two options.spx.gamma-migration.* topics are the exception to the plain-delete note above.)
# options.spx.gamma-migration.current is compacted for the same reason as gex.strike: it is a
# last-value-per-chain LIVE view, so a consumer that starts late needs the newest record per key and
# nothing else. options.spx.gamma-migration.scoring is deliberately NOT compacted — every record
# there is a distinct (call, horizon) observation and compaction would discard the accumulated
# evidence the topic exists for.
# options.spx.vol-premium.ivrv is compacted and MUST stay at ONE partition: it is a single ordered
# series whose consumers use a per-session frame ordinal to decide whether two readings were
# observed back to back, and a second partition would interleave two tasks' ordinals with no way to
# re-order them. The service creates it and refuses to boot on any other partition count, but it is
# declared here as well so cleanup-topics does not delete it as undeclared while the service is
# running — boot-time enforcement cannot protect a topic from being removed underneath a live pod.
# Rebuildable on reset: it carries only the current session's readings.
# options.spx.spot-vol-regime.current is compacted: single-key ("SPX") latest-regime view; the
# .events stream stays plain delete. Both are 1 partition by design (one key, ordering matters).
# market.spx.market-carry-service.current is compacted (last-value carry view, 32 partitions to match
# the es.* variant). It MUST be pre-created here, not left for market-carry-service to lazily create:
# databento-gex declares a Kafka Streams GLOBAL STORE (gex-market-carry-store) backed by this topic,
# and a global store FAILS HARD at init ("no partitions available for topic ...") if the topic is
# absent — it does not retry like a normal consumer. After every clean-slate the topics are wiped, so
# if databento-gex boots before market-carry-service recreates this topic, the gex pod crash-loops and
# no GEX is produced (verified dev 2026-08-18). Pre-creating it removes the boot-order race in both envs.
OPTIONS_EDGE_COMPACTED_TOPICS="corridor-gauge-state options.spx.gamma-migration.current options.databento.oi.nowcast.by-strike options.es-strike-intel-spx-aligned options.databento.pace.mission options.databento.market-pressure.mission options.databento.sandwich.mission options.databento.volume.state.compacted options.databento.maxpain options.spx.vix-option-inteligence-service.current market.spx.market-carry-service.current options.spx.greek-move-auth.current options.spx.mission-control.current options.rewind.journal options.databento.gex.strike options.spx.spot-vol-regime.current options.spx.vol-premium.ivrv options.ibkr.gex.strike.shadow options.ibkr.gex.status options.indicators.snapshot.current options.indicators.bootstrap.control"
# options.spx.gamma-migration.scoring is protected here as well as being declared retention=-1
# AND listed in OPTIONS_EDGE_RESET_PRESERVED_TOPICS (retention alone no longer implies preservation):
# cleanup-topics.sh honours THIS regex, and its delete-recreate mode (the Jenkinsfile's default
# when KAFKA_CLEANUP_TOPICS=true) would otherwise drop the accumulated evidence record on an
# ordinary deploy. Retention alone does not save a topic that is deleted outright.
# R-WIRE.2: the pre-open status topic's tombstones must survive >=48h so a restart can always
# reconstruct the window state (apply-topics.sh applies these as delete.retention.ms).
OPTIONS_EDGE_TOPIC_DELETE_RETENTION_OVERRIDES="options.ibkr.gex.status=172800000"

# The two es.options.indicators.* mirrors were protected here by EXACT name on 2026-08-09 as a
# stopgap, because dev and prod disagreed about their shape and one shared declaration would have
# described neither. That drift is now RESOLVED (dev repaired to the frozen contract, see the
# declaration further down), so they are declared instead of name-protected.
# The swap is NOT protection-neutral and the difference is deliberate. This regex is consulted in
# exactly one place — cleanup-topics.sh's KAFKA_DELETE_UNWANTED_TOPICS loop — and declaring a topic
# keeps it out of that loop just as well. But an UNDECLARED topic is also absent from the approved
# list, so it escaped the destructive cleanup loops entirely; a DECLARED one does not, and a
# KAFKA_CLEANUP_TOPICS=true deploy will delete-and-recreate it (or shrink its retention) like any
# other approved topic. Accepted, because es4 holds the source of both topics and neither copy is
# authoritative — but note MM1 commits its offsets on the SOURCE cluster, so a wiped target is NOT
# back-filled: snapshot.current refills from the next produced record, and es.options.indicators.bars
# would simply start its 45-day history again on that env (nothing on prod or dev reads bars).
PROTECTED_TOPIC_REGEX='^(__consumer_offsets|_schemas|__transaction_state|options\.rewind\.(journal|audit)|options\.spx\.gamma-migration\.(scoring|crossings|wall-touch|fragility)|es\.options\.spx\.gamma-migration\.(crossings|wall-touch|fragility)|corridor-gauge-event-log)$|.*-(changelog|repartition)$'

# options.spx.gamma-migration.{current,scoring} are declared here rather than left to the
# service's own ensureTopic so the partition count is a reviewed decision, not a broker default:
# after the re-key one option chain is ONE key, so 4 partitions carry the handful of live expiries
# and nothing is gained by more. `current` is COMPACTED (listed above): it is a last-value-per-chain
# live view, so a late consumer needs the newest record per key and nothing else. `scoring` is
# plain delete on purpose — it is an append-only evidence log where every record is a distinct
# (call, horizon) observation, and compaction would silently discard the record the topic exists
# to accumulate.
#
# --- ES<->SPX basis engine state (design: es_spx_basis_engine) ---
# spx.basis.state holds STATE_CURRENT: the trusted ES-SPX anchor the feed resumes from on boot
# (the watcher assigns TopicPartition(topic, 0) explicitly, so it MUST be single-partition), and
# it must survive indefinitely -> PURE compact + retention -1. Previously undeclared, so every
# env auto-created it with broker defaults (32 partitions, delete): the anchor was unreachable on
# dev and the ES-on-SPX overlay fail-closed with basisState=UNAVAILABLE. Prod's correct topic was
# hand-made during the 2026-07-18 operator bootstrap; this declaration makes it reproducible.
# RESET-PRESERVED topics: data that CANNOT BE REBUILT, so the destructive dev/off-hours resets
# must skip it. Declared explicitly rather than inferred from retention=-1, because those are two
# different statements and conflating them is wrong in both directions:
#
#   retention.ms=-1  = "do not age this out by time"   (a Kafka storage knob)
#   reset-preserved  = "this cannot be reconstructed"  (a semantic claim about the data)
#
# options.spx.spot-vol-regime.current is exactly the case that separates them. Its own declaration
# calls it a single-key ("SPX") latest-regime view, so a consumer joining late must find the newest
# record -- which the 24h delete half destroys over any gap longer than a day, i.e. every weekend.
# It therefore needs retention=-1. It must NOT be reset-preserved: it is live state the service
# republishes seconds after it starts, and dev is entitled to a clean slate.
#
# Deriving preservation from retention=-1 (the previous rule) would have force-preserved it on dev.
#
# es.tape-zones.board is PRESERVED, and it is the one entry here that no local service produces.
# That is precisely why: tape-zones-service runs ONLY on es4, so on prod and dev the board arrives
# by MM1 record-copy and nothing on those clusters can republish it. MM1 commits its offsets on the
# SOURCE cluster, so wiping the TARGET does not make it re-copy anything — auto.offset.reset only
# applies when a group has no committed offset, and this group has one. A purged board therefore
# stays purged until es4 next publishes, i.e. until the next session actually trades: hours over a
# weekend, days over a holiday. Jenkinsfile.es-tape-zones-mirror already reaches this conclusion
# from the other side, which is why its consumer is the only mirror in the repo seeded from
# `earliest` ("across a weekend or a holiday that is hours-to-days of a blank /zones board").
# Preservation here is what keeps cleanup-topics.sh's delete-recreate mode (the Jenkinsfile default
# whenever KAFKA_CLEANUP_TOPICS=true) from deleting an approved topic that cannot be rebuilt.
# The reach of this list is exactly its three consumers — cleanup-topics.sh, offhours-clean-slate.sh
# and (via PRESERVE_TOPICS_REGEX) premarket-reset.sh — all of which match on the name alone. So when
# premarket-reset is pointed at .4, where this name is the SOURCE board rather than a mirror, the
# same entry spares it there too, which is correct for the same reason. It is NOT a blanket es4
# guarantee: scripts/es4/cleanup-es4.sh rebuilds es4 from the declared set and does not read this
# list at all, and cleanup-topics.sh refuses TOPIC_SET=es4 outright.
OPTIONS_EDGE_RESET_PRESERVED_TOPICS="spx.basis.state corridor-gauge-event-log options.spx.gamma-migration.scoring options.spx.gamma-migration.crossings es.options.spx.gamma-migration.crossings options.spx.gamma-migration.wall-touch es.options.spx.gamma-migration.wall-touch options.spx.gamma-migration.fragility es.options.spx.gamma-migration.fragility options.databento.oi.anchor-manifest es.drop.final-summary es.drop.outcome spx.drop.final-summary spx.drop.outcome es.tape-zones.board"
OPTIONS_EDGE_PROD_ONLY_RESET_PRESERVED_TOPICS="underlying.vix.price"
# The other half of the classification. Every topic declared retention.ms=-1 must appear in
# EXACTLY ONE of these two lists, so a future -1 topic cannot be added without someone deciding,
# on the record, whether losing it costs anything. REBUILDABLE means the resets may destroy it
# freely: the producing service reconstructs it, and dev is entitled to a clean slate.
# options.indicators.bootstrap.control is REBUILDABLE by REQUIREMENT, not merely by
# permission: it records that a session backfill already ran for a trade date, and the
# planner treats a COMPLETE manifest as "this session must not replay again". Preserving
# it across a reset that wipes the service's state/checkpoints would therefore BLOCK the
# very backfill the clean slate needs. The two must be destroyed together.
# es.futures.cvd.bars (retention -1) is REBUILDABLE on this broker, on the record: the SPX-side
# copy is an MM1 MIRROR of the es4 source topic (options-edge-deploy#825/#826) — a destructive
# reset loses only the local replica and the mirror re-syncs the full keyed bar history from
# es4, which owns the durable source. Nothing is lost that the mirror cannot restore.
# U16: es.futures.cvd.levels (prod mirror copy) re-fills from es4 via the mirror exactly like
# cvd.bars; options.es-cvd-spx-levels is DERIVED state the aligner re-publishes from the mirrored
# source + basis after any reset (its ownership-then-scan gate handles the empty log).
OPTIONS_EDGE_RESET_REBUILDABLE_TOPICS="options.spx.spot-vol-regime.current options.indicators.bootstrap.control es.futures.cvd.bars es.futures.cvd.levels options.es-cvd-spx-levels"
OPTIONS_EDGE_PURE_COMPACT_TOPICS="spx.basis.state options.databento.oi.anchor-manifest"
# spx.basis.state is read via assign(TopicPartition(topic, 0)) — it is ONLY correct at exactly one
# partition, so an auto-created 32-partition copy must be destructively repaired (and re-seeded).
# options.ibkr.gex.status is read via assign(TopicPartition(topic, 0)) by the pre-open GEX
# service's generation mint-above probe — ONLY correct at exactly 1 partition; and the shadow
# strike topic must stay EXACTLY 32 so the gate-BETA stage flip (shadow -> live-dark on the
# live topic; gate gamma is user visibility only, R-ROLL) cannot change key->partition
# mapping vs the live options.databento.gex.strike:32.
# es.options.indicators.{snapshot.current,bars} are here for the key->partition half of the rule,
# not the assign() half: they are MM1 record-copies of es4 topics, so the target's partition count
# IS the mirrored key mapping. Repairing them destructively is cheap and correct — es4 holds the
# source, and MM1 keeps its offsets there, so a recreated target simply refills from the next
# produced record.
# Every FROZEN mirror target belongs here: its job asserts PARTS=n, but without exact-partition
# membership apply-topics.sh treats the declared count as a FLOOR, so a widened topic reconciles
# clean while breaking the record-copy key->partition mapping. Verified against the live brokers
# (es4 + production) before declaring, so this asserts the shape they already have.
OPTIONS_EDGE_EXACT_PARTITION_TOPICS="spx.basis.state options.ibkr.gex.status options.ibkr.gex.strike.shadow es.options.indicators.snapshot.current es.options.indicators.bars es.futures.cvd es.futures.cvd.bars es.tape-zones.board"
# spx.basis.a1.evidence is an append-only A1 evidence trail: single partition, plain delete, 3d.
# corridor-gauge-event-log = -1 (ETERNAL). It is the SHADOW-MODE acceptance evidence for the
# corridor gauge (CORRIDOR-GAUGE-GATE1.md): every verdict, its +30-min outcome, wall touches,
# episode ends, and the once-per-day SESSION_END that makes "complete sessions" computable from
# the log alone. The UI unlock gate is computed ONLY from this topic; deleting a day of it
# silently un-completes a session and restarts the acceptance clock.
# options.spx.gamma-migration.scoring = -1 (ETERNAL). It is the falsification record for the
# gamma-migration thesis (GMS-R9): one record per directional call per 5/15/30-minute horizon,
# meant to be ACCUMULATED ACROSS SESSIONS so the thresholds can be refitted from evidence rather
# than from the single 2026-07-30 session they were seeded on. A daily wipe would leave it
# permanently one session deep, which is the same as not having built it. Declaring -1 here also
# requires classifying it as reset-preserved or reset-rebuildable (it is PRESERVED), so a
# future reset script cannot quietly start purging it.
# es.tape-zones.board = -1, the SAME number Jenkinsfile.es-tape-zones-mirror reconciles the target
# to and then asserts (`retention.ms=$RET` with RET=-1) before it will write a plist. Declaring the
# topic in OPTIONS_EDGE_TOPICS + OPTIONS_EDGE_COMPACTED_TOPICS but NOT here left it on the
# environment default, and apply-topics.sh's alter_topic_config sets retention.ms unconditionally on
# every declared topic — so an ordinary deploy REVERTED the board from -1 to 24h. That is not a
# cosmetic disagreement: the policy is compact,delete, and the delete half ages whole segments out
# by time no matter what compaction kept, so the board's last record for `ES|<sessionDate>` is gone
# after any gap longer than the retention — every weekend and every holiday, which is exactly the
# blank /zones page the mirror was built to fix. It also breaks the mirror itself: the next install
# hard-fails its own retention assertion against a target the deploy just changed underneath it.
# Two declarations of one contract must not be allowed to disagree; -1 is the one the owner states.
OPTIONS_EDGE_TOPIC_RETENTION_OVERRIDES="options.spx.gamma-migration.crossings=-1 es.options.spx.gamma-migration.crossings=-1 options.spx.gamma-migration.wall-touch=-1 es.options.spx.gamma-migration.wall-touch=-1 options.spx.gamma-migration.fragility=-1 es.options.spx.gamma-migration.fragility=-1 corridor-gauge-event-log=-1 strike-liquidity-heatmap-dashboard=86400000 es.underlying.es.trades=86400000 es.drop.final-summary=-1 es.drop.outcome=-1 spx.drop.final-summary=-1 spx.drop.outcome=-1 es.drop.nowcast=604800000 spx.drop.nowcast=604800000 rates.sofr.databento-sr3-feed-service.history=1800000 spx.basis.state=-1 spx.basis.a1.evidence=259200000 options.spx.gamma-migration.scoring=-1 options.databento.oi.anchor-manifest=-1 options.spx.spot-vol-regime.current=-1 options.indicators.snapshot.current=604800000 options.indicators.bars=3888000000 options.indicators.bootstrap.control=-1 es.options.indicators.snapshot.current=604800000 es.options.indicators.bars=3888000000 es.tape-zones.board=-1 es.futures.cvd.bars=-1 es.futures.cvd=43200000 options.databento.gex.strike.preopen=259200000"

# --- Previously UNDECLARED, broker-auto-created topics (audit 2026-07-30) ---------------
# These are the only application topics on dev that no app creates with an explicit shape:
# they were left to `auto.create.topics.enable`, so each cluster silently stamped them with
# its OWN `num.partitions` default — prod=1, dev=32. That divergence is the same failure the
# spx.basis.state comment above describes, and it is what blocks turning auto-create OFF on
# the dev broker (scripts/kafka/apply-dev-broker-config.sh).
#
# Shapes below are PROD's live values, read from the broker on 2026-07-30 — this declares
# reality, it does not redesign it, and it makes dev converge on prod at its next wipe.
# apply-topics.sh only errors when current < declared (line ~294), and none of these are in
# OPTIONS_EDGE_EXACT_PARTITION_TOPICS, so dev's existing 32-partition copies are left alone
# until a clean recreates them at the declared shape. Verified against the full 123-topic dev
# app-topic set: the other 108 already match prod, i.e. their apps create them explicitly.
#
# es.options.databento.gex.strike is the one entry with no prod counterpart (absent there,
# 2.68M records on dev). Declared at :4 to match its sibling es.options.databento.gex.spxbridge;
# the cost is one empty topic on prod. es4 is unaffected — apply-topics.sh swaps in
# OPTIONS_EDGE_ES4_TOPICS wholesale when TOPIC_SET=es4.
#
# es.options.indicators.{snapshot.current,bars} are the MM1 mirrors of the es4 indicator outputs
# (Jenkinsfile.es-indicator-mirror). Their shape is a FROZEN CONTRACT, stated in three places that
# must agree: 0DTE-INDICATOR-SERVICE-REQUIREMENT.md §7.1/§7.2, the mirror job's own per-topic case
# statement, and this line — snapshot.current 1 partition compact,delete 7d (last-value view keyed
# by symbol), bars 8 partitions plain delete 45d (append-only history).
# Declared 2026-08-09 after repairing a live drift, which is the whole reason they are here: dev
# lost both topics on 2026-08-07 (topicId changed null -> g3_5Pp4w… in the mirror's own producer
# log), the still-running MM1 producer re-created them through `auto.create.topics.enable`, and
# dev's num.partitions=32 + no cleanup.policy + retention.ms=-1 defaults stuck until measured two
# days later. Measured consequence: the sole prod/dev reader (feed-gateway) SURVIVED it — it seeks
# back 5 minutes by TIME across all assigned partitions, and every record carries key "ES", so all
# 8837 records sat in partition 0 and its single-partition offset gate never saw an interleave.
# What did break: the topic was neither compacted nor aged out, i.e. an unbounded log on the broker
# whose runaway growth dev-cleanup.sh's own apply_internal_topic_configs comment records at
# 176.8 GB/hour on 2026-07-30; and the mirror job could not be re-installed at all, because its
# PartitionCount assertion hard-fails against 32.
# Declaring them puts the shape under create-topics/apply-topics instead of leaving it to whichever
# process touches the topic first. BOTH are in OPTIONS_EDGE_EXACT_PARTITION_TOPICS below: that list
# is for fixed key->partition mappings as much as for fixed-partition readers (see the
# options.ibkr.gex.strike.shadow entry), and the mirror job gives the same reason in its own words —
# "a partition-count mismatch would silently re-shard the key->partition mapping mid-stream". An
# install-time assertion in a job nobody re-runs is not enough; this makes the next apply-topics run
# refuse a re-drifted topic instead of accepting 32 as "compatible".
# GMS-R19: the durable crossing log. DELETE-ONLY and declared here rather than left to the
# service's ensureTopic, because it is the LEARNING CORPUS — one record per crossing per phase,
# and its retention must be a decision somebody made, not whatever the broker default happens to
# be on the day a pod first starts. (Its siblings .rotation and .floor-test are NOT declared for
# prod and are auto-created; that is a separate gap, noted not fixed here.)
OPTIONS_EDGE_TOPICS="$OPTIONS_EDGE_TOPICS options.spx.gamma-migration.crossings:4 options.spx.gamma-migration.wall-touch:4 options.spx.gamma-migration.fragility:4"
OPTIONS_EDGE_TOPICS="$OPTIONS_EDGE_TOPICS es.options.indicators.snapshot.current:1 es.options.indicators.bars:8 es.futures.aggressor-flow:1 es.futures.cvd:1 es.futures.cvd.bars:1 es.tape-zones.board:1 es.strike-intelligence-by-strike:32 es.options.databento.gex.spxbridge:4 es.options.databento.gex.strike:4 option-price-behavior-dashboard:1 options.hpsf.latest-signal:1 options.hpsf.market-flow:1 options.hpsf.strike-score:1 options.ibkr.unusualwhales.gex.strike:1 options.ibkr.unusualwhales.gex.strike.history:1 options.spx.strike-invasion.current:1 rates.sofr.databento-sr3-feed-service.current:1 signal-follower.hot-strike:1 strike-intelligence-turn-alert:1 corridor-gauge-state:1 corridor-gauge-event-log:4 underlying.spx.price:1 spx.drop.nowcast:1 spx.drop.final-summary:1 spx.drop.outcome:1"
# underlying.spx.price is compact,delete on prod (last-price-per-key). Declaring it in
# OPTIONS_EDGE_TOPICS alone would apply plain delete and STRIP that compaction — the exact
# trap the options.databento.gex.strike comment at the top of this file warns about.
# es.tape-zones.board is the MM1 mirror of the es4 board (es-tape-zones-mirror). It is
# declared here so cleanup-topics with KAFKA_DELETE_UNWANTED_TOPICS=true keeps it, and
# compacted here because the board is a last-value view keyed ES|<sessionDate> — a plain
# delete copy loses exactly the semantics the /zones page reads. Verified live 2026-08-09:
# 1 partition + compact,delete on BOTH prod and dev, so one declaration fits both.
# es.options.indicators.snapshot.current is compacted for the same reason its es4 original is:
# it is the last-value-per-symbol live view the gateway replays to new WebSocket clients. Its
# sibling es.options.indicators.bars is deliberately NOT here — bars is append-only history and
# compacting it would collapse the series to one bar per key.
# es.futures.aggressor-flow was the live instance of that trap, not a hypothetical one. It has been
# declared in OPTIONS_EDGE_TOPICS since the 2026-07-30 audit but never listed here, while its owner
# creates the target `--config cleanup.policy=compact,delete` (Jenkinsfile.es-futures-flow-mirror)
# and es4 declares the source compacted (OPTIONS_EDGE_ES4_COMPACTED_TOPICS). Every dev/prod deploy
# therefore reconciled it to plain `delete` and stripped the compaction back off. The mirror job
# asserts `cleanup.policy=compact` on the target before it will install, so the two mechanisms were
# already in open contradiction: a deploy would break the next re-install of the mirror.
OPTIONS_EDGE_COMPACTED_TOPICS="$OPTIONS_EDGE_COMPACTED_TOPICS underlying.spx.price spx.drop.final-summary spx.drop.outcome es.tape-zones.board es.options.indicators.snapshot.current es.futures.aggressor-flow es.futures.cvd es.futures.cvd.bars"

# --- VIX feed separation (design VIX-FEED-SEPARATION-DESIGN.md rev 4 §6 — PROD-SCOPED) ---
# These OPTIONS_EDGE_PROD_ONLY_* sets are honored by apply-topics.sh / verify-topics.sh
# ONLY when ENVIRONMENT is EXPLICITLY 'production' (the env var set to that exact value)
# AND TOPIC_SET is the default (non-es4) set. If ENVIRONMENT is unset/empty they are
# SKIPPED with a loud notice (fail-closed) — load-kafka-settings.sh's default-to-production
# is deliberately never trusted here, and the environment is never inferred from a broker
# address. Dev's topic set and policies are untouched (r2 finding 7 / finding 11).
#
# underlying.spx.index.price (declared above, :1): the IBKR SPX cash-index hop topic
# (ibkr-feed dual-produces it to BOTH clusters; each env's databento-feed consumes its LOCAL
# copy as spot tier-1). SINGLE partition on purpose — the feed's replay watermark is the
# partition offset, which is only monotonic at exactly one partition. Plain delete retention.
# underlying.vix.price.shadow: the shadow phase's output topic — plain delete, 1 day.
# U16 (ES-CVD-SPX-LEVELS-DESIGN.md CL-R6, PRODUCTION-ONLY per its L1/M1 scope): the mirrored
# CVD levels source and the SPX-aligned output. Both PURE COMPACT (AA1: the latest attestation
# per key must NEVER age out — delete retention would erase the ownership-then-scan gate's
# baseline), 1 partition frozen (the mirror arm and the aligner assert it).
OPTIONS_EDGE_PROD_ONLY_TOPICS="underlying.vix.price.shadow:1 es.futures.cvd.levels:1 options.es-cvd-spx-levels:1"
# underlying.vix.price (already declared in OPTIONS_EDGE_TOPICS as :1 for every env) is
# PURE compact on prod: the latest VIX price per key must survive indefinitely — a
# compact,delete policy would drop it once the global retention elapsed.
OPTIONS_EDGE_PROD_ONLY_PURE_COMPACT_TOPICS="underlying.vix.price es.futures.cvd.levels options.es-cvd-spx-levels"

# --- PROD-ONLY: topics that must NOT be compacted (archive fidelity) ---
# 2026-08-23..25: the daily Kafka->NAS archive was measurably losing history. The archiver logs it
# per partition, e.g. "options.databento.maxpain p16: 1,483,194 readable of 6,532,474 offsets
# (compacted topic — history is NOT recoverable from it)" — 77% of that partition's history was
# already gone. Compaction keeps only the newest record per key, so an archive taken after the
# cleaner has run can never reconstruct the session.
#
# Removing a name from OPTIONS_EDGE_COMPACTED_TOPICS would change DEV and ES4 too. This list
# SUBTRACTS from that set for production ONLY, using the same explicit ENVIRONMENT=production
# predicate as the merges above, so it fails CLOSED: dev and es4 policies are untouched.
#
# Every entry here carries retention.ms=-1 on prod (verified on the live broker 2026-08-25), which
# is what makes dropping compaction SAFE: nothing ages out, so a late consumer still finds the
# newest record per key — it just reads more to get there.
#
# DELIBERATELY NOT LISTED (compaction is load-bearing because retention is FINITE — the delete half
# would drop the newest record over any gap longer than the window, which is exactly the failure the
# spot-vol-regime note above describes):
#   options.spx.spot-vol-regime.current       retention 24h
#   options.spx.greek-move-auth.current       retention 24h
#   options.databento.volume.state.compacted  retention 336h
# Also not listed: options.databento.oi.shadow.by-strike (absent on prod).
#
# Hard service attestations live OUTSIDE this file and must stay compact or the service crashes on
# boot (PureCompactTopic.ensure, "durable attestation requires exactly 'compact' (AA1)"):
#   options.es-cvd-spx-levels, es.futures.cvd.levels   — es-spx-align-service CrashLoopBackOff 2026-08-24
# spx.basis.state stays PURE compact: it is the anchor the feed resumes from on boot.
# NOT listed and left compacted for now, deliberately — each needs its own decision:
#   corridor-gauge-state          min.cleanable.dirty.ratio=0.01, looks like service state
#   es.tape-zones.board, es.futures.*   MM-mirrored from es4; a prod-only flip here would
#                                       diverge the mirror from its source and is out of scope
OPTIONS_EDGE_PROD_ONLY_UNCOMPACTED_TOPICS="options.spx.gamma-migration.current options.databento.oi.anchor-manifest options.es-strike-intel-spx-aligned options.databento.pace.mission options.databento.market-pressure.mission options.databento.sandwich.mission options.databento.maxpain options.spx.vix-option-inteligence-service.current options.spx.mission-control.current options.rewind.journal options.databento.gex.strike underlying.spx.price options.indicators.bootstrap.control options.databento.oi.nowcast.by-strike options.ibkr.gex.strike.shadow options.ibkr.gex.status"
# Both topics carry a single-partition read contract on prod: partition count must be
# EXACT (not "at least"), enforced by apply AND verify.
OPTIONS_EDGE_PROD_ONLY_EXACT_PARTITION_TOPICS="underlying.vix.price underlying.vix.price.shadow es.futures.cvd.levels options.es-cvd-spx-levels"
# Explicit retention encoding (verify-then-codify, design §6.3): real topic -1 (compact,
# never expires), shadow 86400000 (1d). Kept in a PROD_ONLY overrides var (merged into
# OPTIONS_EDGE_TOPIC_RETENTION_OVERRIDES under the same explicit-production predicate)
# so dev's underlying.vix.price keeps its default retention — dev untouched.
OPTIONS_EDGE_PROD_ONLY_TOPIC_RETENTION_OVERRIDES="underlying.vix.price=-1 underlying.vix.price.shadow=86400000 es.futures.cvd.levels=-1 options.es-cvd-spx-levels=-1"
# NEVER-RECREATE guard (VFS-R8, r2 finding 7): a partition-count mismatch on a listed
# topic is a HARD ERROR in apply-topics.sh EVEN IF KAFKA_RECREATE_MISMATCHED_TOPICS=true —
# a global operator cleanup flag must never be able to destroy the compacted VIX price
# history. Unconditional (protective only; it never mutates anything).
OPTIONS_EDGE_NEVER_RECREATE_TOPICS="underlying.vix.price"
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ES4 TOPIC SET (the es4 broker on 192.168.100.4 — the ES-0DTE environment).
#
# SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH: es4 topics are declared HERE and applied by the SAME
# scripts/kafka/apply-topics.sh that Jenkins uses for dev/prod. They were
# previously hardcoded in scripts/es4/create-es-topics.sh, which drifted from
# this file and encoded the partition/retention contract only in bash arrays.
#
# SCOPED ON PURPOSE: es4 runs ONLY these es.* topics. Applying the SPX
# OPTIONS_EDGE_TOPICS set to the es4 broker would create ~50 unrelated
# options.* topics there. apply-topics.sh selects this set via TOPIC_SET=es4.
#
# Kafka-Streams changelog/repartition topics are NOT listed: the apps create
# them at runtime, and PROTECTED_TOPIC_REGEX keeps them out of destructive
# reconciliation.
# Service OUTPUT topics of the es4 deployments (delta-flow, gex-flow, strike-intelligence,
# option-price-behavior, volume-pace, greek-move-authenticity, option-truth-engine). Declared here so
# the reset recreates them with their REAL partition counts instead of relying on broker auto-create
# (which would silently give them the default). Orphan topics from services that do NOT run on es4
# (ibkr.*, hpsf.*, mission-control, strike-invasion, strike-sr, open-direction, volume-sandwich,
# market-carry) are deliberately EXCLUDED — a reset must not resurrect them.
#
# ⭐PARTITION COUNTS MUST BE THE REAL STEADY-STATE SHAPE, NOT A GUESS OR A "SAFE" SMALL NUMBER.
# apply-topics.sh treats the declared count as a MINIMUM, so an under-declared topic is created
# small, then WIDENED by the owning service's own admin client seconds later. Any Kafka Streams app
# that resolved its source metadata inside that window sizes its repartition/changelog topics to the
# SMALL count and then dies forever on every rebalance with
#     StreamsException: Existing internal topic ...-repartition has invalid partitions: expected: 32; actual: 4
# while the pod still reports 1/1 Running and healthy. That is exactly what happened to
# strike-flow-classifier (and strike-liquidity-heatmap) after the 2026-08-02 clean-reset: the
# contract said es.options.opra.tcbbo:4, the service widened it to 32 at +3m20s, and the classifier
# processed 0 records for 3h with every health signal green. 24 entries were corrected on 2026-08-03
# against BOTH the live es4 broker and prod's shape for the same topic (23 have a prod twin, all 32;
# es.options.databento.gex.spxbridge is es4-native and lives at 32).
# ⭐POLICY for the es4 set: these counts are the EXACT desired shape, not a floor. A clean-reset
# rebuilds the es4 world from this file, so a partition count the file does not record is NOT
# preserved — widening a topic out-of-band on the broker silently reverts at the next reset.
# verify-topic-partition-contract.sh (mode `steady`) fails the reset and the create-topics job on any
# live-vs-declared disagreement, so a deliberate widening must be recorded HERE to survive.
OPTIONS_EDGE_ES4_TOPICS="es.dealer-ledger-calibration-state:32 es.dealer-ledger-outcome-scored:32 es.dealer-ledger-profile:32 es.dealer-ledger-signal-fired:32 es.dealer-ledger-state:32 es.delta-flow-10s:32 es.delta-flow-15m:32 es.delta-flow-1m:32 es.delta-flow-30s:32 es.delta-flow-5m:32 es.delta-flow-by-strike:32 es.delta-flow-by-trade:32 es.delta-flow-corrections:32 es.delta-flow-dashboard:32 es.delta-flow-diagnostics:32 es.delta-flow-session:32 es.option-price-behavior-by-strike:32 es.option-price-behavior-dashboard:4 es.option-price-behavior-by-option:32 es.option-price-behavior-session:32 es.options.databento.control:4 es.options.databento.directional-pressure:32 es.options.databento.display.gamma.history:4 es.options.databento.display.volume.current:32 es.options.databento.display:32 es.options.databento.events.raw:32 es.options.databento.gex.flow.10s:32 es.options.databento.gex.flow.15m:32 es.options.databento.gex.flow.1m:32 es.options.databento.gex.flow.5m:32 es.options.databento.gex.flow.by-strike:32 es.options.databento.gex.flow.dashboard:32 es.options.databento.gex.flow.session:32 es.options.databento.gex.magnet:32 es.options.databento.gex.spxbridge:32 es.options.databento.gex.strike-lifecycle:32 es.options.databento.gex.strike.history:32 es.options.databento.gex.strike.preopen:32 es.options.databento.gex.strike:32 es.options.databento.market-pressure.mission:32 es.options.databento.maxpain:32 es.options.databento.normalized:32 es.options.databento.pace.mission:32 es.options.databento.pace.rank:32 es.options.databento.pace:32 es.options.databento.raw:32 es.options.databento.sandwich.mission:32 es.options.databento.strike-flow.strike.avro:32 es.options.databento.strike-flow:32 es.options.databento.seller-activity:32 es.options.databento.volume.state.compacted:32 es.options.es.option-truth-engine-service.by-strike:32 es.options.es.spread-skew.current:32 es.options.es.spread-skew.events:32 es.options.hpsf.dlq:4 es.options.marketdata.selection:4 es.options.opra.tcbbo:32 es.options.spx.vix-option-inteligence-service.current:4 es.options.spx.greek-move-auth.current:32 es.options.spx.greek-move-auth.events:32 es.reversal.final-summary:1 es.reversal.outcome:1 es.reversal.strength:1 es.reversal.verdicts:1 es.futures.aggressor-flow:1 es.futures.cvd:1 es.futures.cvd.bars:1 es.futures.cvd.levels:1 es.signal-follower.hot-strike:1 es.strike-intelligence-by-strike:32 es.strike-intelligence-dashboard:32 es.strike-intelligence-turn-alert:4 es.strike-liquidity-heatmap-bucket:32 es.strike-liquidity-heatmap-dashboard:32 es.options.indicators.snapshot.current:1 es.options.indicators.bars:8 es.options.indicators.repartition:4 es.options.indicators.bootstrap.control:1 es.tape-zones.board:1 es.tape-zones.cells:4 es.underlying.es.price:4 es.underlying.es.trades:4 es.underlying.spx.price:4 es.underlying.vix.price:4 es.close.direction.signal:4 es.close.direction.state:1 es.market.spx.market-carry-service.current:32 es.options.databento.gex.oi-status:32 es.options.hpsf.audit:4 es.options.hpsf.exit-signal:4 es.options.hpsf.latest-signal:4 es.options.hpsf.market-flow:4 es.options.hpsf.strike-score:4 es.options.spx.strike-invasion.current:4 es.options.spx.strike-sr.current:4 es.heartbeats:1"
# compact,delete (compaction plus the global retention floor)
# es.tape-zones.{cells,board}: tape-zones-service creates BOTH via processing-common
# changelogTopicConfigs (compact,delete) — cells at 4 partitions, board at 1 — so the
# declared shape here matches exactly what the service's ensure-topic would create
# (es4 topic contract: EXACT desired shape, not a floor). The cells topic additionally
# carries message.timestamp.type=LogAppendTime; apply-topics.sh has NO per-topic config
# mechanism beyond cleanup/retention/delete.retention, so that config is DECLARED by the
# service at ensure-topic time (TapeZonesRuntime.start reconciles it on every boot, and
# its EOD validator asserts it) rather than here.
OPTIONS_EDGE_ES4_COMPACTED_TOPICS="es.options.databento.pace.mission es.options.databento.market-pressure.mission es.options.databento.sandwich.mission es.options.databento.volume.state.compacted es.options.databento.maxpain es.options.databento.seller-activity es.dealer-ledger-calibration-state es.underlying.es.price es.underlying.vix.price es.options.spx.vix-option-inteligence-service.current es.options.spx.greek-move-auth.current es.reversal.final-summary es.reversal.outcome es.futures.aggressor-flow es.futures.cvd es.futures.cvd.bars es.close.direction.state es.market.spx.market-carry-service.current es.drop.final-summary es.drop.outcome es.options.indicators.snapshot.current es.options.indicators.bootstrap.control es.tape-zones.cells es.tape-zones.board"
# U16 (ES-CVD-SPX-LEVELS-DESIGN.md AA1): es.futures.cvd.levels is PURE compact on the SOURCE too.
# OPTIONS_EDGE_ES4_COMPACTED_TOPICS resolves to compact,delete, whose delete half would age out the
# latest attestation — and the producer's ownership-then-scan gate READS THAT RECORD BACK at
# startup, so losing it is a fail-closed startup, not a cosmetic drift. The mirror job additionally
# asserts POLICY=compact against the source in its preflight, so compact,delete here would hard-fail
# the install.
OPTIONS_EDGE_ES4_PURE_COMPACT_TOPICS="es.futures.cvd.levels"
# Single-partition read contracts: es.reversal.* and es.signal-follower.* are
# consumed with single-partition ordering. Broker auto-create would give them
# the default 4 partitions, and ensure_topic_custom never repaired that — this
# is exactly the drift that made an auto-created topic unusable.
OPTIONS_EDGE_ES4_EXACT_PARTITION_TOPICS="es.reversal.verdicts es.reversal.strength es.reversal.final-summary es.reversal.outcome es.signal-follower.hot-strike es.futures.aggressor-flow es.futures.cvd es.futures.cvd.bars es.futures.cvd.levels es.close.direction.state es.heartbeats es.tape-zones.board es.options.indicators.snapshot.current es.options.indicators.bars"
# --- Topics es-feed-gateway BLOCKS on, previously left to broker auto-create (2026-07-31) ------
# es-feed-gateway resolves the FULL topic list of each of its three consumers (state, avro-live,
# alerts) at startup and waits on partitionsFor() for every one. A single missing topic makes the
# consumer throw TopicMetadataTimeoutException and restart on a 30s loop forever, so the board
# stays blank even though the chain data is arriving normally.
#
# Auto-create hid this: the gateway's own metadata request conjured whatever was missing. Turning
# it off on the es4 broker (#670) exposed 13 undeclared topics and blanked es.fullfunding.nl for
# ~40 minutes on 2026-07-31 until they were created by hand. Hand-created topics do not survive a
# clean-reset — declaring them here is what makes the fix durable.
#
# Most of these belong to services in ES4_KEEP_DOWN (volume-sandwich, mission-control,
# unusualwhales), so nothing ever produces to them. They still have to EXIST: the gateway blocks
# on topic metadata, not on data. Shapes are prod's live values, read from the broker, except the
# es4-native es.open-direction.* which follow their sibling es.close.direction.signal at :4.
OPTIONS_EDGE_ES4_TOPICS="$OPTIONS_EDGE_ES4_TOPICS es.open-direction.forecast:4 es.open-direction.outcome:4 es.open-direction.status:4 es.options.databento.volume-sandwich.current:32 es.options.databento.volume-sandwich.alerts:32 es.options.ibkr.display:32 es.options.ibkr.pace:32 es.options.ibkr.pace.rank:32 es.options.ibkr.unusualwhales.gex.strike:1 es.options.ibkr.unusualwhales.gex.strike.history:1 es.options.ibkr.volume-sandwich.current:32 es.options.ibkr.volume-sandwich.alerts:32 es.options.spx.mission-control.current:32 es.options.spx.gamma-migration.current:4 es.options.spx.gamma-migration.scoring:4"

# es-feed-gateway BLOCKS on these at startup (FeedGatewayService topic-metadata wait) and the
# reversal hunt topics are its command/state plane. They were live on es4 only because the broker
# auto-created them; once auto-create was turned off, a clean-reset wiped them and nothing put them
# back, so the gateway avro consumer died every 30s with TopicMetadataTimeoutException listing
# es.options.ibkr.directional-pressure. Partition counts match what es4 actually ran.
OPTIONS_EDGE_ES4_TOPICS="$OPTIONS_EDGE_ES4_TOPICS es.options.spx.gamma-migration.crossings:4 es.options.spx.gamma-migration.wall-touch:4 es.options.spx.gamma-migration.fragility:4"
OPTIONS_EDGE_ES4_TOPICS="$OPTIONS_EDGE_ES4_TOPICS es.options.spx.gamma-migration.floor-test:4 es.options.spx.gamma-migration.rotation:4 es.options.ibkr.directional-pressure:32 es.reversal.hunt.alerts:1 es.reversal.hunt.commands:1 es.reversal.hunt.state:1 es.reversal.hunt.status:1"
# es.options.spx.mission-control.current is compact,delete on prod (last-value-per-key); an
# OPTIONS_EDGE_ES4_TOPICS-only entry would create it plain-delete and strip that compaction.
# gamma-migration mirrors its prod pair: .current is a last-value-per-chain LIVE view, so a
# consumer that starts late needs the newest record per key and nothing else; .scoring is
# deliberately NOT compacted — every record there is a distinct (call, horizon) observation
# and compaction would discard the accumulated evidence the topic exists for.
# es.option-price-behavior-by-option is a latest-value-per-option view and its owner creates it
# compact,delete (scripts/kafka/run-dev-timewarp-replay.sh: `ensure_topic
# option-price-behavior-by-option 32 compact,delete`; prod runs it compact,delete live because
# prod does not declare it, so apply-topics leaves it alone). es4 DOES declare it, so omitting
# it here made create-topics actively RECONCILE THE COMPACTION AWAY — verified live on .4 as
# plain delete, with the tell-tale min.cleanable.dirty.ratio=0.01 left behind (Codex).
OPTIONS_EDGE_ES4_COMPACTED_TOPICS="$OPTIONS_EDGE_ES4_COMPACTED_TOPICS es.options.spx.mission-control.current es.options.spx.gamma-migration.current es.option-price-behavior-by-option"

# es.tape-zones.board = -1 on es4 for the same reason the dev/prod declaration carries it, applied
# to the SOURCE copy. scripts/es4/create-es-topics.sh runs the same apply-topics.sh with
# KAFKA_TOPIC_RETENTION_MS=43200000, and alter_topic_config writes retention.ms on every declared
# topic, so without this line the es4 create-topics job set the source board to 12h. The board is
# compact,delete (declared in OPTIONS_EDGE_ES4_COMPACTED_TOPICS), and the delete half ages segments
# out by time regardless of compaction — 12h does not survive a single overnight, let alone a
# weekend. Jenkinsfile.es-tape-zones-mirror asserts `retention.ms=-1` against the SOURCE in its
# Preflight, before it asserts anything about the target, so the es4 job was arming a hard failure
# of the mirror install as well as expiring the board .4 itself serves.
OPTIONS_EDGE_ES4_TOPIC_RETENTION_OVERRIDES="es.futures.cvd.bars=-1 es.futures.cvd=43200000 es.futures.cvd.levels=-1 es.reversal.verdicts=604800000 es.reversal.strength=172800000 es.options.indicators.snapshot.current=604800000 es.options.indicators.bars=3888000000 es.options.indicators.bootstrap.control=-1 es.signal-follower.hot-strike=604800000 es.tape-zones.board=-1 es.options.databento.gex.strike.preopen=259200000"
